---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Documentation" description="Learn Kōshi's standalone CSS grid API, columns, spans, gaps, offsets, Flexbox layouts, and responsive composition behavior.">
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="docs-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Kōshi / Reference 001</span>
      <h1 class="display">Documentation.</h1>
      <p class="lead">The essentials of Kōshi's framework-independent CSS grid. Designed to be understood, copied, and adapted.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="action action-primary" href="/downloads/koshi.css" download="koshi.css">Download koshi.css ↓</a>
        <a class="action action-outline" href="https://github.com/kalebberry/koshi">Source on GitHub ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="docs-tutorial-banner">
        <div class="tutorial-banner-content">
          <span class="eyebrow">STEP-BY-STEP TUTORIAL</span>
          <h2>Building an Editorial Website with Kōshi</h2>
          <p>Follow a comprehensive hands-on walkthrough constructing an editorial journal from scratch—from fluid mastheads and multi-row magazine spreads to subgrid card baselines.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="action action-primary" href="/docs/tutorial/">Start Tutorial →</a>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="docs-layout">
      <nav class="docs-toc" aria-label="Documentation sections">
        <a href="/docs/tutorial/" class="toc-tutorial-link">★ Editorial Tutorial →</a>
        <span class="eyebrow">ON THIS PAGE</span>
        <a href="#system">Understanding the system</a>
        <a href="#installation">Installation & cascade layers</a>
        <a href="#containers">Containers</a>
        <a href="#columns">Columns & spans</a>
        <a href="#subgrid">Subgrid alignment</a>
        <a href="#gaps">Gutters</a>
        <a href="#offsets">Offsets</a>
        <a href="#responsive">Responsive compositions</a>
        <a href="#ratios">Aspect ratios</a>
        <a href="#visualizer">Lattice visualizer</a>
        <a href="#flex">Flexbox & intrinsic grids</a>
        <a href="#utilities">Other utilities</a>
      </nav>
      <article class="docs-body">
        <section id="system" class="docs-system">
          <span class="eyebrow">01 / THE FOUNDATION</span>
          <h2>Understanding the system</h2>
          <p>Think of a row as twelve equal parts. A block takes a share of that row: <strong>6 + 6</strong> makes two halves, <strong>8 + 4</strong> makes a main area and sidebar, and <strong>4 + 4 + 4</strong> makes three equal columns. Kōshi accounts for the space between blocks using CSS Grid's native gaps.</p>
          <div class="docs-twelve" aria-label="Twelve equal columns">
            {Array.from({ length: 12 }, (_, i) => <span>{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>)}
          </div>
          <p class="docs-small-note">Twelve tracks represent the whole row. The numbers describe proportions, not pixel widths.</p>

          <h3>Three ways to divide the same space</h3>
          <div class="docs-examples">
            <div class="docs-example">
              <div class="docs-example-top"><span>01 / BALANCED</span><strong>6 + 6</strong></div>
              <div class="kos-grid docs-block-grid">
                <div kos-col-span="6" class="docs-block">06 / 12</div>
                <div kos-col-span="6" class="docs-block docs-block--light">06 / 12</div>
              </div>
              <pre><code>{`<div class="kos-grid">
  <div kos-col-span="6">Left</div>
  <div kos-col-span="6">Right</div>
</div>`}</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-example">
              <div class="docs-example-top"><span>02 / ASYMMETRIC</span><strong>8 + 4</strong></div>
              <div class="kos-grid docs-block-grid">
                <div kos-col-span="8" class="docs-block">08 / 12</div>
                <div kos-col-span="4" class="docs-block docs-block--light">04 / 12</div>
              </div>
              <pre><code>{`<div class="kos-grid">
  <main kos-col-span="8">Main</main>
  <aside kos-col-span="4">Aside</aside>
</div>`}</code></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-example">
              <div class="docs-example-top"><span>03 / EVEN RHYTHM</span><strong>4 + 4 + 4</strong></div>
              <div class="kos-grid docs-block-grid">
                <div kos-col-span="4" class="docs-block">04 / 12</div>
                <div kos-col-span="4" class="docs-block docs-block--light">04 / 12</div>
                <div kos-col-span="4" class="docs-block">04 / 12</div>
              </div>
              <pre><code>{`<div class="kos-grid">
  <div kos-col-span="4">One</div>
  <div kos-col-span="4">Two</div>
  <div kos-col-span="4">Three</div>
</div>`}</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p><strong>No <code>kos-cols="12"</code> required.</strong> A direct child with <code>kos-col-span</code> tells Kōshi to use twelve proportional tracks. Without spans, the grid stays automatic. You can still explicitly set <code>kos-cols</code> when you want a different fixed track count.</p>

          <h3>Build an editorial composition</h3>
          <p>Combine rows to create a larger structure. The example below uses two independent grids inside <code>.kos-composition</code>: a wide feature beside supporting copy, followed by three equal blocks. The container query stacks the blocks when the composition becomes narrow.</p>
          <div class="docs-composition-demo">
            <div class="kos-composition">
              <div class="kos-grid docs-block-grid">
                <div kos-col-span="8" class="docs-block docs-block--feature"><span>FEATURE / 08</span><strong>Space shapes the story.</strong></div>
                <div kos-col-span="4" class="docs-block docs-block--light docs-block--feature"><span>TEXT / 04</span><strong>A considered balance.</strong></div>
              </div>
              <div class="kos-grid docs-block-grid">
                <div kos-col-span="4" class="docs-block">01 / 04</div>
                <div kos-col-span="4" class="docs-block docs-block--light">02 / 04</div>
                <div kos-col-span="4" class="docs-block">03 / 04</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <pre><code>{`<section class="kos-composition">
  <div class="kos-grid">
    <div kos-col-span="8">Feature</div>
    <div kos-col-span="4">Supporting copy</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kos-grid">
    <div kos-col-span="4">One</div>
    <div kos-col-span="4">Two</div>
    <div kos-col-span="4">Three</div>
  </div>
</section>`}</code></pre>
          <p class="docs-small-note">Resize the browser to see the composition adapt. The breakpoint is based on its container width, not only the viewport.</p>

          <h3>Automatic layout versus proportional layout</h3>
          <p>For cards that should fit as space allows, leave off span attributes. Kōshi uses <code>auto-fit</code> and <code>--kos-grid-min-item-size</code>. Add spans when the relationship between blocks matters.</p>
          <div class="kos-grid docs-auto-demo" style="--kos-grid-min-item-size: 9rem; --kos-gutter: .75rem">
            <div class="docs-block">AUTO / 01</div>
            <div class="docs-block docs-block--light">AUTO / 02</div>
            <div class="docs-block">AUTO / 03</div>
          </div>
          <pre><code>{`<div class="kos-grid" style="--kos-grid-min-item-size: 9rem">
  <article>Card one</article>
  <article>Card two</article>
  <article>Card three</article>
</div>`}</code></pre>
          <p class="docs-small-note">Use automatic grids for flexible collections; use spans for deliberate 12-part compositions. Both are plain CSS.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="installation">
          <h2>Installation & cascade layers</h2>
          <p>Download the standalone CSS file and serve it from your project. Kōshi requires no framework, JavaScript, or build step.</p>
          <pre><code>{`<link rel="stylesheet" href="/downloads/koshi.css" />`}</code></pre>
          <p>For an Astro project, you can instead import the source stylesheet directly from <code>src/styles/koshi.css</code>. The Composition Lab itself uses Vue, but the grid system does not.</p>
          <h3>Cascade Layer Integration</h3>
          <p>Kōshi's rules are enclosed in <code>@layer kos-grid</code>. This allows modern web applications using CSS cascade layers to integrate Kōshi into their layer priority hierarchy with zero specificity conflicts:</p>
          <pre><code>{`/* Define your application's cascade layer order */
@layer reset, kos-grid, components, utilities;

@import url("/downloads/koshi.css") layer(kos-grid);`}</code></pre>
          <p>Standalone unlayered stylesheets can override Kōshi rules naturally without resorting to <code>!important</code>.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="containers">
          <h2>Containers</h2>
          <p><code>.kos-container</code> centers content and applies a maximum width. Choose a width with the <code>container-type</code> attribute.</p>
          <pre><code>{`<div class="kos-container">Default width</div>
<div class="kos-container" container-type="narrow">Narrow</div>
<div class="kos-container" container-type="wide">Wide</div>
<div class="kos-container" container-type="full-bleed">Full bleed</div>`}</code></pre>
          <p>Default maximum widths are 75rem (default), 48rem (narrow), and 90rem (wide). Edge gutters scale continuously via <code>clamp(1rem, 3.5vw, 3.5rem)</code> without abrupt media-query jumps. Maximum widths and offsets can be customized with CSS custom properties.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="columns">
          <h2>Columns & spans</h2>
          <p>By default, <code>.kos-grid</code> creates an intrinsic auto-fit layout. Adding <code>kos-col-span</code> to a direct child automatically switches the grid to twelve proportional tracks, without needing <code>kos-cols="12"</code>. Use <code>kos-cols</code> to explicitly choose a fixed track count from 1 to 12 (plus widescreen 16).</p>
          <pre><code>{`<div class="kos-grid" kos-cols="12">
  <article kos-col-span="8">Main</article>
  <aside kos-col-span="4">Aside</aside>
</div>`}</code></pre>
          <p>Explicit column counts remain fixed unless you opt into a responsive composition context. Narrow viewports may need an appropriate responsive wrapper.</p>

          <h3>Beyond 12 Columns: Arbitrary Tracks</h3>
          <p>Need 16 columns for widescreen dashboards, 24 for dense Swiss typography, or an unusual number of tracks? Kōshi provides two ways to break out of the 12-column foundation without SCSS or build steps:</p>
          
          <h4>1. Universal CSS Variable Pipeline (All Browsers)</h4>
          <p>Set <code>--kos-cols</code> on the grid and <code>--kos-col-span</code> on any item. This works in 100% of browsers today with zero dependencies:</p>
          <pre><code>{`<!-- 16-column widescreen dashboard -->
<div class="kos-grid" style="--kos-cols: 16">
  <main style="--kos-col-span: 11">Main content (11 of 16)</main>
  <aside style="--kos-col-span: 5">Sidebar (5 of 16)</aside>
</div>`}</code></pre>

          <h4>2. Progressive Enhancement with Typed <code>attr()</code> (Chrome 133+)</h4>
          <p>In browsers supporting modern <strong>CSS Values and Units Level 5</strong>, Kōshi automatically parses integer attribute values natively without hardcoded classes:</p>
          <pre><code>{`<!-- Automatically resolves dynamic integer counts in modern browsers -->
<div class="kos-grid" kos-cols="16">
  <div kos-col-span="10">10 tracks</div>
  <div kos-col-span="6">6 tracks</div>
</div>`}</code></pre>
          <p class="docs-small-note">For guaranteed cross-browser consistency across legacy Safari and Firefox, use the <code>style="--kos-cols: N"</code> custom property pattern for arbitrary tracks beyond 12.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="subgrid">
          <h2>Subgrid alignment</h2>
          <p>
            When building cards side-by-side, differing headline lengths and paragraph copy usually push action buttons down unevenly. Native CSS Subgrid solves this by letting nested card elements participate directly in the parent grid's tracks.
          </p>
          <p>
            Add <code>kos-subgrid</code> (or <code>kos-subgrid="rows"</code>) along with <code>kos-row-span="3"</code> to each card. Notice in the live example below how every headline row, body text block, and bottom action link locks onto the exact same horizontal alignment across all three columns—regardless of how much text is inside:
          </p>

          <div class="docs-subgrid-demo">
            <div class="kos-grid" kos-cols="3">
              <article kos-col-span="1" kos-row-span="3" kos-subgrid class="docs-subgrid-card">
                <h4>01 / Concise Thought</h4>
                <p>A compact single-sentence thought.</p>
                <a href="#subgrid" class="docs-subgrid-action">Explore track ↗</a>
              </article>
              <article kos-col-span="1" kos-row-span="3" kos-subgrid class="docs-subgrid-card">
                <h4>02 / Variable Multi-Line Headline Across Columns</h4>
                <p>Card descriptions and headings frequently vary in length. Subgrid guarantees that neighboring rows expand to match the tallest sibling automatically.</p>
                <a href="#subgrid" class="docs-subgrid-action">Explore track ↗</a>
              </article>
              <article kos-col-span="1" kos-row-span="3" kos-subgrid class="docs-subgrid-card">
                <h4>03 / Balanced Baseline</h4>
                <p>The action links below are perfectly locked to the same horizontal line.</p>
                <a href="#subgrid" class="docs-subgrid-action">Explore track ↗</a>
              </article>
            </div>
          </div>

          <pre><code>{`<div class="kos-grid" kos-cols="3">
  <!-- Each card spans 3 rows and participates in parent row tracks -->
  <article kos-col-span="1" kos-row-span="3" kos-subgrid class="card">
    <h4>Short Title</h4>
    <p>Compact copy.</p>
    <a href="#">Action ↗</a>
  </article>

  <article kos-col-span="1" kos-row-span="3" kos-subgrid class="card">
    <h4>Much Longer Headline Across Multiple Lines</h4>
    <p>Longer body copy that expands row 2 for all cards...</p>
    <a href="#">Action ↗</a>
  </article>

  <article kos-col-span="1" kos-row-span="3" kos-subgrid class="card">
    <h4>Balanced Form</h4>
    <p>Aligned automatically via native CSS Subgrid tracks.</p>
    <a href="#">Action ↗</a>
  </article>
</div>`}</code></pre>
          <p class="docs-small-note">Subgrid requires the element to span multiple tracks on the parent grid (e.g. <code>kos-row-span="3"</code>). Use <code>kos-subgrid="cols"</code> to inherit column tracks instead, or <code>kos-subgrid="both"</code> for full 2D track synchronization.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="gaps">
          <h2>Gutters</h2>
          <p>Gaps default to 1.5rem. Use the gap utilities or override <code>--kos-gutter</code> for custom spacing.</p>
          <pre><code>{`<div class="kos-grid kos-gap-4" kos-cols="3">...</div>
<div class="kos-grid" kos-cols="12" style="--kos-gutter: 2rem">...</div>`}</code></pre>
          <p>Available utilities are <code>.kos-gap-0</code>, <code>.kos-gap-2</code>, <code>.kos-gap-4</code>, <code>.kos-gap-6</code>, and <code>.kos-gap-8</code>. Native CSS Grid fractional tracks account for gutters automatically.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="offsets">
          <h2>Offsets</h2>
          <p>Use <code>kos-offset</code> values 1–6 to set a child's starting grid line. Offsets are explicit positions, not additive margins: ensure the offset and span fit within the grid.</p>
          <pre><code>{`<div class="kos-grid" kos-cols="12">
  <article kos-col-span="6" kos-offset="3">Shifted content</article>
</div>`}</code></pre>
          <p>For example, offset 3 starts on grid line 4; with span 6 it ends at line 10. An offset plus a span that exceeds the grid can create implicit tracks, so choose combinations deliberately.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="responsive">
          <h2>Responsive compositions</h2>
          <p>Add <code>.kos-composition</code> around one or more fixed grids to opt into container-query responsiveness. Direct child columns stack into a single column according to the container's width, not the global viewport.</p>
          <pre><code>{`<section class="kos-composition">
  <div class="kos-grid" kos-cols="12">
    <div kos-col-span="7">Visual</div>
    <div kos-col-span="5">Copy</div>
  </div>
</section>`}</code></pre>
          <h3>Tiered Collapse Breakpoints</h3>
          <p>Control exactly when stacking occurs with <code>kos-collapse</code>:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><code>kos-collapse="sm"</code>: Collapses at <strong>32rem</strong> (compact widgets, card containers).</li>
            <li>Default / <code>kos-collapse="md"</code>: Standard collapse at <strong>48rem</strong>.</li>
            <li><code>kos-collapse="lg"</code>: Collapses early at <strong>64rem</strong> (dense multi-track layouts).</li>
            <li><code>kos-collapse="none"</code>: Prevents stacking entirely, preserving fixed columns at all container sizes.</li>
          </ul>
          <pre><code>{`<!-- Small container collapse (e.g. sidebar widget) -->
<section class="kos-composition" kos-collapse="sm">
  <div class="kos-grid" kos-cols="3">...</div>
</section>

<!-- Fixed layout that never collapses -->
<section class="kos-composition" kos-collapse="none">
  <div class="kos-grid" kos-cols="4">...</div>
</section>`}</code></pre>
          <p>This opt-in behavior leaves other fixed grids unchanged and respects container boundaries wherever the composition is embedded.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="ratios">
          <h2>Aspect ratio framing</h2>
          <p>Prevent Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS) and maintain visual cadence using <code>kos-ratio</code>. Useful on image containers, video embeds, and editorial hero slots.</p>
          <div class="docs-ratio-demo">
            <div class="kos-grid" style="--kos-grid-min-item-size: 130px; --kos-gutter: 14px">
              <div kos-ratio="16/9" class="docs-ratio-card">
                <strong>16 / 9</strong>
                <span>Widescreen · 1.77:1</span>
              </div>
              <div kos-ratio="4/3" class="docs-ratio-card">
                <strong>4 / 3</strong>
                <span>Classic · 1.33:1</span>
              </div>
              <div kos-ratio="1/1" class="docs-ratio-card">
                <strong>1 / 1</strong>
                <span>Square · 1:1</span>
              </div>
              <div kos-ratio="silver" class="docs-ratio-card">
                <strong>Silver</strong>
                <span>Compact · 1:1.414</span>
              </div>
              <div kos-ratio="golden" class="docs-ratio-card">
                <strong>Golden</strong>
                <span>Portrait · 1.618:1</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <pre><code>{`<!-- Media container with aspect-ratio framing -->
<div kos-ratio="16/9">
  <img src="/visual.webp" alt="Editorial scene" />
</div>

<!-- Silver ratio portrait / column card (1:1.414) -->
<article kos-col-span="4" kos-ratio="silver">
  <img src="/portrait.webp" alt="Feature portrait" />
</article>

<!-- Golden ratio framing (1.618:1) -->
<article kos-col-span="4" kos-ratio="golden">
  <img src="/editorial.webp" alt="Editorial feature" />
</article>`}</code></pre>
          <p>Available values: <code>16/9</code>, <code>4/3</code>, <code>1/1</code> (or <code>square</code>), <code>3/4</code>, <code>golden</code> (1.618:1), and <code>silver</code> (1:1.414). Inner media automatically expands to fill the container with <code>object-fit: cover</code>.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="visualizer">
          <h2>Lattice visualizer (Debug mode)</h2>
          <p>Kōshi includes a zero-JavaScript visual debugging mode. Add the <code>kos-debug</code> attribute to any grid or composition to project subtle <em>Shu-iro</em> (traditional Japanese cinnabar red) lattice guides and automatic track badges across children.</p>
          <div class="docs-composition-demo">
            <div class="kos-composition" kos-debug>
              <div class="kos-grid docs-block-grid" kos-cols="12">
                <div kos-col-span="8" class="docs-block docs-block--feature"><span>FEATURE / 08</span><strong>Lattice visualizer active.</strong></div>
                <div kos-col-span="4" class="docs-block docs-block--light docs-block--feature"><span>SIDEBAR / 04</span><strong>Automatic badge tags.</strong></div>
              </div>
              <div class="kos-grid docs-block-grid" kos-cols="12">
                <div kos-col-span="4" class="docs-block">01 / 04</div>
                <div kos-col-span="4" class="docs-block docs-block--light">02 / 04</div>
                <div kos-col-span="4" class="docs-block">03 / 04</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <pre><code>{`<!-- Add kos-debug while designing; remove for production -->
<section class="kos-composition" kos-debug>
  <div class="kos-grid">
    <div kos-col-span="8">Feature</div>
    <div kos-col-span="4">Sidebar</div>
  </div>
</section>`}</code></pre>
          <p>Every column card automatically displays its track span (e.g. <code>08 / 12</code>) in a non-destructive overlay that doesn't affect page layout or pointer events.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="flex">
          <h2>Flexbox & intrinsic grids</h2>
          <p>Use <code>.kos-flex-grid</code> for a wrapping Flexbox layout. Its twelve-column span calculations account for gutters; a full-width <code>kos-col-span="12"</code> occupies one row.</p>
          <pre><code>{`<div class="kos-flex-grid">
  <div kos-col-span="6">Left</div>
  <div kos-col-span="6">Right</div>
</div>`}</code></pre>
          <p>For an intrinsic CSS Grid layout, omit <code>kos-cols</code> and child <code>kos-col-span</code> attributes. Kōshi uses auto-fit with a configurable minimum item size.</p>
          <pre><code>{`<div class="kos-grid" style="--kos-grid-min-item-size: 14rem">
  <article>One</article>
  <article>Two</article>
  <article>Three</article>
</div>`}</code></pre>
        </section>
        <section id="utilities">
          <h2>Other utilities</h2>
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>API</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>kos-cols="1"–"12" | "16"</code></td>
                <td>Fixed column track counts</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>--kos-cols / --kos-col-span</code></td>
                <td>Arbitrary custom column and span counts (e.g. 16, 24) without SCSS</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>kos-row-span="1"–"6"</code></td>
                <td>Span CSS Grid rows</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>kos-subgrid="rows|cols|both"</code></td>
                <td>Inherit parent grid tracks (CSS Subgrid)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>kos-collapse="sm|md|lg|none"</code></td>
                <td>Container query collapse breakpoint for .kos-composition</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>kos-ratio="16/9|4/3|1/1|3/4|golden|silver"</code></td>
                <td>Aspect ratio framing and anti-CLS media fitting (including Silver 1:1.414)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>kos-debug</code></td>
                <td>Project pure-CSS lattice guides and column span badges</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>kos-order="-4"–"4"</code></td>
                <td>Set visual order</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>kos-grow="0"–"3"</code></td>
                <td>Flex grow values in a flex grid</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>.kos-sidebar-grid</code></td>
                <td>Sidebar plus main content</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>.kos-masonry-grid</code></td>
                <td>Multi-column masonry with progressive enhancement to native CSS Grid masonry</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>.kos-cq</code></td>
                <td>Named CSS query container</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>.kos-flow</code></td>
                <td>Vertical rhythm between children</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p>See the source stylesheet for the complete available selectors. Kōshi is currently an early release; the API may evolve.</p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
